        <div class="settings-panel-container">
            <div class="settings-panel @UI.PanelService.Panels[1].PanelStatus">
                <h3 class="text-center">BeeHive Settings</h3>
                <br />
                <div class="settings-scrollable-section">
                    <div class="">
                        <label class="form-check-label" for="timerBeingUsed">
                            <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" value="" id="timerBeingUsed" @bind="BeeHiveController.Instance.TimerIsBeingUsed">
                            Use Timer (<span style="color: red;"> WARNING: Changing from "unselected" to "selected" will force a game restart. </span>)
                        </label>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="settings-bottom-container">
                    <div class="settings-close" @onclick="(()=>UI.DeactivatePanel(1))">
                        Close
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="introduction-panel-container">
            <div class="introduction-panel @UI.PanelService.Panels[11].PanelStatus" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="introduction-title">
                <div class="introduction-header">
                    <button type="button" class="introduction-back" title="Back" aria-label="Back" @onclick="(()=>UI.DeactivatePanel(11))">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </button>
                    <h2 id="introduction-title">Welcome to the Hive!</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="introduction-scrollable-section">
                    <div class="">
                        In this game, you are the Queen Bee.
                        <br/><br/>
                        Your goal is to maximize honey production while 
                        preventing the economic collapse of your hive!
                        <br /><br />
                        As the Queen Bee, you lay an egg once every few days. Then each egg is nursed 
                        by your nurse bees. Egg nurses help the egg mature. The more egg nurses there are, 
                        the faster each egg matures. Once mature, each egg hatches and a new bee is born!
                        <br /><br />
                        But each newborn bee is a SLACKER! It is your job as Queen Bee to boss 
                        the bees of your hive around and make sure they do their work.
                        <br /><br />
                        You can order bees to make honey, collect nectar or nurse eggs. Once a bee
                        has an assigned job, it works that same job forever. (Bees don't switch 
                        professions, in case you didn't know.)
                        <br /><br />
                        Watch out though! Each bee can do their job only if there is enough honey 
                        in the vault, and each bee eats before they do their job each day. This
                        means in the same day, some bees may eat enough to work while other bees that come 
                        after them might not have enough to eat if the vault becomes empty in the middle of the day.
                        <br /><br />
                        Bees eat in this order: (1) Queen Bee, (2) Unassigned bees, 
                        (3) worker bees (*in the order they were assigned their jobs)
                        <br /><br />
                        You start out with 1 of each kind of worker bee (3 kinds) and zero eggs.
                        <br /><br />
                        Alternatively, you can hire someone else to boss the bees around for you so that 
                        all you have to do is manage the worker assignments. The guy you hired doesn't like 
                        to wait around though - he's very consistent at bossing around bees! 
                        This version of the game can be enabled/disabled via the gear icon (settings).
                        <br /><br />
                        The Queen Bee, who eats first, has to have enough honey to eat each day or else 
                        she dies (and the hive goes bankrupt).
                        <br /><br />
                        Will your hive thrive? Will your hive survive!? You decide!!!
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="introduction-bottom-container">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="(()=>UI.DeactivatePanel(11))">
                        Boss Around Some Bees
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</ProjectsPageTemplate>

@code {
    private EWorkerType workerType = EWorkerType.HoneyMaker;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        UI.ActivatePanel(11);  // Introduction panel
        BeeHiveController.Instance.BeeHive.Queen.OnTimerInterval += UpdateV3View;
        UI.OnUiServiceChanged += UpdateThisComponent;
    }
    void IDisposable.Dispose()
    {
        BeeHiveController.Instance.BeeHive.Queen.OnTimerInterval -= UpdateV3View;
        UI.OnUiServiceChanged -= UpdateThisComponent;
    }

    private void UpdateThisComponent(string meaningless) =>
        StateHasChanged();

    private void UpdateV3View(bool timerInterval)
    {
        BeeHiveView.Instance.UpdateAssignButtons();
        StateHasChanged();
    }
    private void Reset()
    {
        BeeHiveController.Instance.Reset();
        BeeHiveView.Instance.UpdateAssignButtons();
    }
}

